# BB child thread orchestration

Before spawning or retrying bb child threads, **discover exact model slugs** — never pass display names.

## Preflight (required)

```bash
bb status --json
bb provider list
bb provider models acp-opencode | rg -i "qwen|mlx|omlx"
bb provider models acp-cursor
```

## Model slugs (this project)

| Use case | Provider | Model slug |
|----------|----------|------------|
| Small/scoped tasks | `acp-opencode` | `omlx/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-MLX-3bit` |
| Larger tasks (if needed) | `acp-cursor` | `composer-2.5` |

**Wrong:** `--model "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B 3-bit UD-MLX"` (display name → thread error)
**Right:** `--model omlx/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-MLX-3bit`

## Spawn pattern

```bash
bb thread spawn \
  --parent-self \
  --project proj_qj64jbvqgf \
  --provider acp-opencode \
  --model omlx/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-MLX-3bit \
  --title "Short task title" \
  --prompt "Scoped prompt with paths and acceptance criteria."
```

For bigger tasks, swap provider/model:

```bash
--provider acp-cursor --model composer-2.5
```

## Retry failed threads

1. Inspect: `bb thread log <id> --format json --limit 30` — confirm root cause:
   - Bad model slug: `execution.model` shows display name instead of slug
   - Context overflow on `tell`: `Prompt too long … exceeds max context window`
2. **Prefer fresh spawn** over `bb thread tell` when the failed thread has bloated history or hit provider/context errors.
3. If retrying in-place, pass explicit model slug:

```bash
bb thread tell <id> "Continue: …" --model omlx/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-MLX-3bit
```

4. Wait: `bb thread wait <id> --status idle --timeout 600`
5. Review: `bb thread output <id>`

If opencode hits context limits on a larger task, escalate:

```bash
bb thread spawn ... --provider acp-cursor --model composer-2.5
```

## Parent responsibilities

- Scope prompts narrowly (one task, explicit file paths, out-of-scope list)
- Wait for child completion before merging
- If child fails, fix model slug and retry — do not silently redo work in the parent unless the child is unrecoverable
